/Title (When an astronomy catalog announces thousands of newly identified worlds, the public imagines camera lenses photographing distant continents. In reality, the transit method records a tiny silhouette: a planet passes between its host star and the observatory line of sight, blocking a fractional percentage of starlight at exact periodic intervals.)
